/-! Let S(n) = Sum_k binomial(n,k) binomial(2n+k,k), so that a(n) = binomial(2n,n) S(n). By creative
telescoping, c2(n) S(n+2) + c1(n) S(n+1) + c0(n) S(n) = 0 with c2 = 4(n+2)(17n+11)(2n+3),
c1 = -1207(n+2)^3 + 2840(n+2)^2 - 1897(n+2) + 360 and c0 = 2(17n+28)(2n+1)(n+1): with
H(n,j) = Q(n,j+1) binomial(n+1,j) binomial(2n+j+1,j), where Q(n,k) is a quadratic polynomial in k, the
summand of this recurrence at k = j+1, multiplied by (n+1)(2n+4)(2n+3)(2n+2), equals
H(n,j+1) - H(n,j); this is a polynomial identity modulo the ratio relations between the binomial
coefficients involved. The recurrence for a(n) follows from
(n+1) binomial(2n+2,n+1) = 2(2n+1) binomial(2n,n). -/

